ற்றொடு","gloss":"with the elephant"}],"gloss":"with the elephant","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேல்","parts":[{"text":"வேல்","lemma":"vēl","gloss":"spear"}],"gloss":"spear"},{"surface":"துரந்து","parts":[{"text":"துரந்து","lemma":"turantu","gloss":"having thrown"}],"gloss":"having thrown"},{"surface":"இனியே","parts":[{"text":"இனி","lemma":"iṉi","gloss":"now"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"now indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தன்னும்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"taṉ","gloss":"himself"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"himself too"},{"surface":"துரக்குவன்","parts":[{"text":"துரக்குவன்","lemma":"turakkuvaṉ","gloss":"he will throw/drive"}],"gloss":"he will throw"},{"surface":"போலும்","parts":[{"text":"போலும்","lemma":"pōlum","gloss":"it seems"}],"gloss":"it seems"},{"surface":"ஒன்னலர்","parts":[{"text":"ஒன்னலர்","lemma":"oṉṉalar","gloss":"enemies"}],"gloss":"enemies"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எஃகுடை","parts":[{"text":"எஃகுடை","lemma":"எஃகுடை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வலத்தர்","parts":[{"text":"வலத்தர்","lemma":"வலத்தர்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மாவொடு","parts":[{"text":"மாவொடு","lemma":"மாவொடு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பரத்தரக்","parts":[{"text":"பரத்தரக்","lemma":"பரத்தரக்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"கையின்","parts":[{"text":"கை","lemma":"kai","gloss":"hand"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"with/by"}],"gloss":"with his hand"},{"surface":"வாங்கி","parts":[{"text":"வாங்கி","lemma":"vāṅki","gloss":"having pulled/grabbed"}],"gloss":"having grabbed"},{"surface":"தழீஇ","parts":[{"text":"தழீஇ","lemma":"taḻīi","gloss":"having embraced"}],"gloss":"having embraced"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மொய்ம்பின்","parts":[{"text":"மொய்ம்பு","lemma":"moympu","gloss":"strength"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with strength"},{"surface":"ஊக்கி","parts":[{"text":"ஊக்கி","lemma":"ūkki","gloss":"having exerted/raised"}],"gloss":"having exerted"},{"surface":"மெய்","parts":[{"text":"மெய்","lemma":"mey","gloss":"body"}],"gloss":"body"},{"surface":"கொண்டனனே","parts":[{"text":"கொண்டு","lemma":"koḷ","gloss":"having taken"},{"text":"அனன்","lemma":"aṉaṉ","gloss":"he"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"he received"}]}],"literal":"Blue girdle flower-filled garment / peacock-feather chaplet great-natured warrior / against-coming elephant-with spear-thrown now-indeed / himself-too will-throw it-seems, enemies / spear-having strong-men horses-with swarming / hand-with grabbing embracing / strength-with exerting body-on received-indeed","translation":"The noble warrior, wearing a blue sash, a flower-patterned garment, and a chaplet of peacock feathers, has already hurled his spear at the charging elephant. Now, it seems he will hurl himself too! As the enemies, strong men armed with spears, rushed forward with their horses, he grabbed them with his hands, embraced them, and with exerted strength, received their weapons directly on his body.","modern":"நீல நிறக் கச்சையும் பூக்கள் நிறைந்த ஆடையும் அணிந்து, பீலி மாலையைத் தலையில் சூடிய பெருந்தகைமை கொண்ட வீரன், தன் மேல் வந்த யானையின் மீது தன் வேலை எறிந்துவிட்டான். இனி அவன் தன்னையே பகைவர் மேல் எறிந்துவிடுவான் போலத் தோன்றுகிறது. பகைவர்கள் வேலேந்தி குதிரைகளோடு பரவி வர, அவர்களைத் தன் கைகளால் பற்றித் தழுவி, தன் வலிமையால் அவர்களைத் தாங்கி, அவர்களின் ஆயுதங்களைத் தன் உடலிலேயே ஏற்றுக்கொண்டான்.","explanation":"An onlooker on the battlefield praises the extreme valor of a warrior. This poem belongs to the tumpai tiṇai (battlefield warfare) and the theme erumai maṟam, which depicts the fierce, unyielding bravery of a single warrior who stands like a wild buffalo blocking the enemy's advance. The warrior, adorned with a blue sash and peacock feathers, has already thrown his spear at an oncoming war elephant. Left weaponless, he does not retreat; instead, as enemy cavalry and infantry swarm him, he grabs them with his bare hands and embraces them in close combat. With exerted strength, he takes their spear-thrusts directly onto his own chest, sacrificing himself to stop their advance. The key words are 'மறவன்' (warrior), 'வேல்துரந்து' (having thrown the spear), and 'மெய்க்கொண்டனனே' (he received them on his body).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.9],[0.9,1.4],[1.4,1.4],[1.4,1.4],[1.4,2.4],[2.4,2.6],[2.6,2.9],[2.9,4.5],[4.5,4.67],[4.67,4.9],[4.9,5.9],[5.9,6.37],[6.37,7.47],[7.53,7.7],[7.7,8.1],[8.1,8.4],[8.4,8.7],[8.7,8.7],[8.7,9.0],[9.0,11.5],[11.5,11.6],[11.6,11.9],[11.9,13.4],[13.4,13.4],[13.4,13.9],[13.9,14.15]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.8],[1.03,1.37],[1.37,1.6],[1.6,1.6],[1.6,3.1],[3.1,3.3],[3.3,3.6],[3.6,4.9],[5.09,5.47],[5.66,6.6],[6.6,7.0],[7.0,7.27],[7.27,7.8],[7.8,8.9],[8.9,9.4],[9.7,10.1],[10.1,10.8],[10.8,11.2],[11.2,12.0],[12.0,12.8],[12.8,13.0],[13.0,13.3],[13.3,14.13],[14.13,14.13],[14.13,15.38],[15.38,15.8]]}}